rtain 2014-2016 Forester, 2008-2016 Impreza sedans, 2012-2016 Impreza station wagons, 2008-2014 WRX sedans (including STI), and 2013-2017 Crosstrek vehicles.  Exposure to certain contaminants may cause the brake light switch to malfunction, preventing the brake lights from illuminating and also preventing keyless ignition vehicles from starting and CVT/automatic transmissions from being able to be shifted out of Park.","consequence":"Brake lights that do not illuminate properly will not alert other drivers that the vehicle is slowing or stopping, increasing the risk of crash.","remedy":"Subaru will notify owners, and dealers will replace the brake light switch, free of charge.  The recall began April 15, 2019.  Owners may contact Subaru customer service at 1-844-373-6614.  Subaru's number for this recall is WUE-90.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1303530,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V149000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":24,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2008","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2009","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2010","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2012","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2009","make":"SUBARU","model":"WRX"},{"year":"2013","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2011","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2008","make":"SUBARU","model":"WRX"},{"year":"2014","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"},{"year":"2014","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2011","make":"SUBARU","model":"WRX"},{"year":"2015","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"},{"year":"2014","make":"SUBARU","model":"WRX"},{"year":"2016","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2010","make":"SUBARU","model":"WRX"},{"year":"2012","make":"SUBARU","model":"WRX"},{"year":"2013","make":"SUBARU","model":"WRX"},{"year":"2015","make":"SUBARU","model":"IMPREZA"},{"year":"2016","make":"SUBARU","model":"CROSSTREK"},{"year":"2013","make":"SUBARU","model":"CROSSTREK"},{"year":"2016","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"},{"year":"2017","make":"SUBARU","model":"CROSSTREK"},{"year":"2015","make":"SUBARU","model":"CROSSTREK"},{"year":"2014","make":"SUBARU","model":"CROSSTREK"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"13V159000","received":"2013-04-24","manufacturer":"Subaru of America, Inc.","component":"EQUIPMENT","summary":"Subaru is recalling certain model year 2014 Forester vehicles manufactured from January 2013 through March 2013. The backing for the carpeted floor mats was not manufactured to specification.  As a result, the floor mats may curl when exposed to heat.","consequence":"Curling of the driver side floor mat could distract the driver and/or interfere with proper operation of one or a combination of, the vehicle's clutch, brake, and accelerator pedals.  Brake or accelerator pedal interference may result in very high vehicle speeds and make it difficult to stop the vehicle, which could cause a crash.","remedy":"Subaru will notify owners, and dealers will replace each of the vehicle's four (4) carpeted floor mats with new ones.  These services will be performed free of charge.  Subaru issued an interim notification during April 2013.  Notification that the remedy is now available was mailed to owners on June 5, 2013.  Owners may contact Subaru at 1-800-782-2783.  Subaru's recall campaign number is WQH-44.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":10137,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=13V159000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":1,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
